+### The false-reject rate reached 0/241 because the generator changed, not the tool
+
+Recorded here because it is the number most likely to be quoted out of the v1.1
+release page, and quoting it without this sentence would be a false claim about
+the tool.
+
+v1.0 measured false reject `1/241 (0.4 %)` on the fourth draw. v1.1 measures
+`0/241 (0.0 %)` on the fifth. The single case is **`S00709`**, which v1.0's own
+`benchmarks/hard/README.md` diagnosed at length as a **mislabel** — the tool was
+right, the expectation was computed at an operating point the case does not
+declare — and explicitly declined to fix, because fixing it meant moving the
+ratings cases across the whole draw. `5cd1b75` ("ratings are sized at the
+operating point the run reaches, not the asymptote") is that fix. **No code
+changed. The tool's answer is the same before and after.**
+
+It is the fifth correction to this generator, and it is the cleanest example of
+why the hold-out exists: a headline rate went to zero because the benchmark came
+round to the tool's answer. Every other figure held across a draw that rewrote
+1744 of 2000 case files, which is the reassuring half — the regeneration touched
+what it claimed to and nothing else.
+
